      against: [
        { p: "AIS-189 compliance interpretation is still evolving — over-engineering for a draft understanding is risky", why: "ARAI's interpretation of AIS-189 requirements for specific ECA configurations is not yet fully settled; compliance investment based on an incorrect interpretation wastes development cost.", sowhat: "Participate in ARAI AIS-189 technical working group sessions to shape the interpretation; invest compliance engineering after the specific requirements are confirmed." },
        { p: "IP protection for ECA software in India is improving but still incomplete — reverse engineering risk", why: "ECA software compiled for Bosch platforms could be reverse-engineered by competitors; India's IP enforcement for embedded software is stronger than before but not at European levels.", sowhat: "Implement hardware security modules (HSMs) in all Bosch ECA platforms to prevent software extraction; file key ECA algorithm patents in India jurisdiction." },
        { p: "Liability for ECA failures affecting safety systems is legally complex under India Consumer Protection Act", why: "If a Bosch ECA failure disables multiple vehicle systems simultaneously, Consumer Protection Act liability could be invoked against both Bosch and the OEM.", sowhat: "Define ECA failure mode liability clearly in supply agreements; maintain product liability insurance covering multi-system ECA failure scenarios." },
      ],
